>> 5. Have pet steal money from floor and drop it outside the shop.

>Too late. You have to do that _before_ you convert your credit to money
>(using steps 1-3 above), because that process has negative returns. So you
>have to do it with cloned credit to get something out of it.

No you don't. Once the real money leaves the shop and is redropped on the
floor you get more credit. The order doesn't matter too much. If you run
it the way that I've outlined above you get done faster because you're
converting more cash into credit each each time. A quick example.

I walk into a wand shop with no wands and $300. 

1. Drop the $300 for $300 in credit.
2. Pick up wands that I can afford and purchase.
3. Resell. Yes it's for for less money. But I didn't spend money. I spent
credit. So I get back say $125 for the $250 in wands that I bought.
4. Now drop the $125. The pet has $425 to steal now instead of $300. 

It hasn't cost me anything. "My" $300 stake is still on the floor. Now
I've added $125 from the shopkeeps pocket to it. When the pet steals the
$425, I now have more capital to purchase more wands to resell.

The objective is to get as much cash on the floor as possible.

